== A1. told ONCE that X is v1 (tau_told = 0.3), then m other TRUE statements about X; v1 never denied ==
   m    W+     W-      f      c      e     | corrected (open world, chi_told = 0): f, c, e
    0   0.30   0.00   1.000  0.231  0.615   |  1.000 0.231 0.615
    1   0.30   0.18   0.619  0.326  0.539   |  1.000 0.231 0.615
    2   0.30   0.35   0.464  0.393  0.486   |  1.000 0.231 0.615
    3   0.30   0.49   0.379  0.442  0.446   |  1.000 0.231 0.615
    5   0.30   0.75   0.286  0.512  0.390   |  1.000 0.231 0.615
   10   0.30   1.28   0.190  0.613  0.310   |  1.000 0.231 0.615
   20   0.30   2.10   0.125  0.705  0.236   |  1.000 0.231 0.615
   50   0.30   3.80   0.073  0.804  0.157   |  1.000 0.231 0.615
   -> after TWO unrelated statements the design holds the uncontradicted fact at f < 1/2.

== A2. X has K permanent true properties; every statement names one of them (uniform); 4000 statements ==
   K   f*(theory)  f_sim   c_sim   e_sim   e_sim(threshold variant: only e>1/2 counts as predicted)
    2    0.618      0.618   0.999   0.618    0.618
    3    0.500      0.500   0.999   0.500    0.505
    5    0.390      0.390   0.998   0.390    0.500
   10    0.282      0.282   0.998   0.282    0.500
   50    0.133      0.131   0.995   0.133    0.499
   -> every one of these facts is TRUE and was never contradicted; the design ends convinced (c ~ 1)
      that each holds with frequency f*(1/K) < 1/2 for K >= 4; with the threshold variant it ends at
      e ~ 1/2 with c ~ 1, which §2.6 reports as 'conflict'.

== B. explicit denial.  Stream: 'X v1' once, then n times 'X not v1' (symbols X, not, v1 in one moment) ==
   The only route to w- in §2.5 is 'predicted, did not occur'.  In a denial v1 DOES occur.
   n denials   W+(X->v1)  W-(X->v1)   e(X->v1)
       0         0.30       0.00      0.615
       1         0.60       0.00      0.688
       2         0.90       0.00      0.737
       5         1.80       0.00      0.821
      10         3.30       0.00      0.884
   -> ten denials raise e(X->v1) from 0.615 to 0.884.  A told contradiction has no path to W-,
      while silence (part A) has one.  Both are the wrong way round.

== C. trust in a 100% honest teller.  The teller told all K true properties of each of 200 objects once.
      Then the senses show an object with ONE of its true properties per moment (4000 moments). ==
   Design: sensed occurrence on a told tie confirms the teller; 'predicted, did not occur' refutes it.
   K   tau_honest(C3 literal: w- += e_trust)  tau_honest(plain: w- += 1)  theory f*(1/K), 1/K | tau_liar(literal)
    2         0.618                           0.500                  0.618   0.500 |    0.008
    5         0.390                           0.200                  0.390   0.200 |    0.008
   10         0.282                           0.100                  0.282   0.100 |    0.008
   50         0.133                           0.020                  0.133   0.020 |    0.008
   -> the trust earned by an honest teller measures how many properties the objects have (the co-mention
      rate), not honesty.  For K >= 4 an honest teller ends BELOW 1/2.
   corrected, same stream: the sight channel's completeness is its own repetition rate; a glimpse of another
   aspect is then not a refutation.  Precision A of each teller, refereed by sight (prior 1.3/0.7):
   K    chi_sight (true 1/K)   A_honest   A_liar
    2        0.474 (0.500)        0.927     0.014
    5        0.161 (0.200)        0.884     0.017
   10        0.069 (0.100)        0.832     0.022
   50        0.011 (0.020)        0.608     0.067

